"""Owner-side campaign world (family ``ndfeb_c5_campaign_v1``): one hidden draw from a named C5 package.

A world is a single posterior draw of the owner-built physics tool C5 (Dynamical's model, fitted to RPI's released
records): a density mechanism and one of its stored draws; a coercivity mechanism, a load-timing explanation and one
of their stored draws, chosen with the package's own weights and draw-assignment functions; the package's declared C5
layers at those indices; and a per-world seed. The package is loaded from its directory, and every file is checked
against the sha256s the world names (the package's own `load(manifest=...)` check runs as well).

Per-draw values come from the package's own internal functions evaluated at the world's indices. This module adds
only: the single-draw evaluation helper (`World.evaluate`), the declared body-to-body and measurement noise, the
deterministic per-world streams (preparation effects, body effects, measurement draws) and the companion's existing
request/delivery contract (shared with ``ndfeb_magnetic_workflow_v1``). It is an owner-side native provider
dependency, never an investigator answer key, and it reads no RPI result beyond what the package contains.
"""
